**Personal Digital Library App — Requirements**

Build a personal book cataloging web app (Progressive Web App) that works on Android and browser, stores data on Google Drive/cloud, and works offline.

**UI language:** Italian and English, user-switchable via a dropdown menu showing each option with its flag icon and language name (e.g. 🇮🇹 Italiano / 🇬🇧 English). All labels, buttons, and fixed field values (e.g. Cartaceo, Posseduto, Letto) translate with the selected UI language.

**App Layout:**
- **Top app bar:** hamburger menu icon (opens side menu), app title, search icon, sort icon, view-toggle icon.
- **Hamburger menu** (side drawer) contains: UI language switch, Import/Export, Google Drive connection/sync. Add a Show/Hide Stats toggle.
- **Main page** has two tabs: **Shelves** and **Books**. The selected tab's view is shown below.
- Both views share: a path/breadcrumb row, an item count, and a filter icon; each has its own sort and filter options.
- **Shelves view:** list of shelves, each showing a thumbnail icon, shelf name, book count, and a 3-dot menu (rename/delete/merge actions).
Clicking a shelf opens that shelf's Books view, filtered to just that shelf's books, updating the breadcrumb path (e.g. Home > Shelf name) and item count accordingly.
- **Books view:** books grouped by author surname under section labels, with an A–Z fast-scroll index on the side. Each row shows cover thumbnail, title, author, and status badges (reading status, format).
- **Add a book:** three methods — search online (Title/ISBN), scan ISBN via camera, or add manually. Reachable via a floating "+" button.

**Book fields** (in this exact order):
Title, Author, Publisher, Series, Volume, Language, Format, Reading Status, Ownership, Shelf, ISBN

- Each book belongs to **exactly one** shelf.
- Hidden fields (not shown in UI) store cover image data.
- Cover image is fetched automatically by ISBN, trying sources in this order: **Google Books → Open Library → Amazon (search by ISBN, then by Title if ISBN fails)**.
- **Note:** Amazon has no free public search API like Open Library/Google Books — using it requires an Amazon Associates account with the Product Advertising API, or another workaround. Flag this for the build chat when this step is reached.
- If no image is found from any source, show the placeholder icon.

**Reading Status:** dropdown options are Letto / In lettura / Da leggere only. On **import**, the values "Si", "Sì", "X" (case insensitive) are recognized as aliases for "Letto" — not shown as manual entry options.

**Ownership** options: Posseduto / In prestito / Non posseduto.

**Format** options: Cartaceo / Ebook / Audiolibro.

**Language** options: Italiano / English / Français / Deutsch / Español.

**Stats counters** (top of screen):
- Total books
- Read books (Reading Status = Letto, or Si/Sì/X on import)
- Owned books (Ownership = Posseduto)
- On loan books (Ownership = In prestito)
Stats counters section — note that visibility is controlled by this toggle (hidden by default state: visible, unless toggled off).

**Book list:**
- Search box (by Title/Author)
- Sort by Title, Author, or Reading Status
- Shelf filter chips at top of list
- Each book card shows badges for reading status, ownership, format, language, shelf

**Book management:**
- Add, edit, and delete books
- Add book modal: two tabs (search by Title / search by ISBN), searches Google Books API (then Open Library, then Amazon as fallback per above), shows cover/author/year, clicking a result pre-fills Title, Author, Publisher, ISBN, Language, and cover image if available; all fields remain manually editable after pre-fill
- ISBN barcode scanning via device camera as an additional way to add a book

**Shelf management:**
- Add and remove shelves dynamically
- Rename shelves inline by clicking the name
- Shelf names are case insensitive
- Renaming into a duplicate name triggers a confirmation dialog: "Sì, unisci" / "No, modifica nome", offering to merge the two shelves

**Import/Export:**
- Export to XLSX, columns in this exact order: Titolo, Autore, Editore, Serie, Volume, Lingua, Formato, Stato lettura, Posseduto, Scaffale, ISBN, Copertina (URL)
- Import from XLSX using either full set of headers below (not mixed):

| Field | Italian | English |
|---|---|---|
| Title | Titolo | Title |
| Author | Autore | Author |
| Publisher | Editore | Publisher |
| Series | Serie | Series |
| Volume | Volume | Volume |
| Language | Lingua | Language |
| Format | Formato | Format |
| Reading Status | Stato lettura | Reading Status |
| Ownership | Posseduto | Ownership |
| Shelf | Scaffale | Shelf |
| ISBN | ISBN | ISBN |
| Cover Image | Copertina | Cover Image |

- On import: validate columns; show a clear error listing any missing columns; mention any unrecognized columns
- Cover Image column is optional on import — if present, its URL is used; if absent/empty, the image is fetched via the ISBN fallback chain above
- If valid, show a success confirmation with book count and any new shelves to be created before importing
- New shelves found in import are added automatically
- If an imported book's ISBN already exists in the library, ask the user per duplicate whether to keep the existing entry or update it with the imported data

**UI/UX:**
- All confirmation dialogs use in-app modals (never browser confirm/alert)
- No limit on number of books